# THE ORCHESTRATOR'S OWN RUNTIME (003). Both directories are named by this repository's
# `agent-protocol.json` — 'orchestrator.state' and 'orchestrator.workdir.worktrees' — so
# they exist on every box that raises a role here, and neither is ever committed.
# Left untracked they are not merely noise: `workingTreeState` counts untracked as DIRTY
# (a `pull --ff-only` refuses over an untracked file), and a dirty tree makes
# `selfRestartVerdict` STAND before any form of repair is chosen. A box serving this
# repository would then meet every merge into `main` with a daemon that stops repairing
# itself and says 'dirty' about its own workspaces. `runtime-ignored.test.ts` holds this.
.orchestrator/
.worktrees/
